<newsitem itemid="103784" id="root" date="1996-10-08" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: St Ives books year profit rise.</title>
<headline>St Ives books year profit rise.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>53 weeks to August 2</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		28.74		  vs 25.36</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 10.0		   vs 8.5</p>
<p> Pretax		     42.2		   vs 35.5</p>
<p> Turnover		   329.0		  vs 264.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Printing group St Ives Plc said that &quot;overall, given the upturn in in consumer spending in the U.K, the outlook is encouraging.&quot;  </p>
<p> Operating result	 41.5		   vs 34.0</p>
<p> Exceptional		nil		    vs nil</p>
<p> Interest (receivable)  0.8		    vs 1.524</p>
<p> Tax			  13.5		   vs 10.3</p>
<p> Net taxed		  28.7		   vs 25.2</p>
<p> Retained		   18.7		   vs 16.7</p>
<p> Pay date		   December 4</p>
<p> Div registration date  October 22</p>
<p> Ex-div date		Nov 11 1996</p>
<p>NOTE - The 53 weeks to August 2 1996 is compared to 52 weeks to July 28, 1995.</p>
</text>
